its old, single, legacy\n`module.audioFile` field (e.g. `audio/n1-maths-01.mp3` — no `-01/-02/-03` suffix) — a URL the segmented\nplayer never looks up. So \"download for offline\" was caching audio under a key the player would never\nfind at playback time.\n\nThe claimed fix: `getAudioUrlsForModule()` now returns `module.segments[].audioFile` (all of them, in\norder) for any formal module that has a non-empty `segments` array, falling back to the legacy single\n`module.audioFile` only when a module has no `segments` (author's claim: none currently lack them — all\n359 formal modules have `segments`). `getAudioEntriesForGradeBand()`'s per-item `moduleId` labelling was\nalso changed: previously only vocational multi-lesson modules got a `-01/-02/...` suffix on `moduleId`;\nnow any module yielding more than one URL gets the suffix, so the fix doesn't create 3 identically-\nlabelled download-list entries per formal module.\n\n## Your job — verify or refute, with specifics\n\n1. Read `app/app.js`: `getAudioUrlsForModule` (search for that exact function name), `isVocationalModule`,\n   `getAudioEntriesForGradeBand`, `prepareDownloadSession`, `deleteAudioForCompletedModules`,\n   `resolveAudioSourceForPath`, `getFormalSegmentAudioFile`, `loadFormalSegmentAudio`. Confirm:\n   - `getAudioUrlsForModule` returns the 3 segment `audioFile` values (in `segments` array order) for a\n     formal module with `segments`, the single legacy `audioFile` for one without, and is unchanged for\n     vocational modules (still reads `module.lessons[].audioFile`).\n   - Every URL `getAudioUrlsForModule` can return for a formal module is a string that\n     `resolveAudioSourceForPath`/`getFormalSegmentAudioFile` would actually request at playback time for\n     that same module — i.e. the download-time key space and the playback-time lookup key space are the\n     *same* strings, not just structurally similar. Look for any subtle mismatch: string case, leading\n     slash, `audio/` prefix present/absent, index base (0 vs 1), zero-padding (`-01` vs `-1`), etc.\n   - `getAudioEntriesForGradeBand`'s new `moduleId` suffix logic (`urls.length > 1 ? id + \"-\" + padded\n     index : id`) doesn't collide with any *other* real ID already in `content.json` (e.g. could\n     `n1-maths-01-02` collide with a real module or lesson id elsewhere in the corpus?).\n   - `deleteAudioForCompletedModules` (cache cleanup when a module is marked passed) — confirm it now\n     deletes all 3 real segment cache entries for a completed formal module, not just one, and doesn't\n     error or leave orphaned cache rows.\n   - Any other function in `app/app.js` that reads `module.audioFile` directly for a formal/non-vocational\n     module (grep for `.audioFile` and `module.audioFile` broadly) that might still assume the old\n     single-file model and was missed by this fix — this is the main thing worth hunting for.\n\n2. Read `app/content.json` (large file — you may `grep`/spot-check rather than load it whole): confirm a\n   sample of formal modules' `segments[].audioFile` values actually follow the\n   `audio/<moduleId>-01.mp3` / `-02.mp3` / `-03.mp3` naming the code assumes, and that `module.audioFile`\n   (the legacy field) is still present and unchanged on those same modules (it should not have been\n   touched by this fix — content.json was not supposed to change for this bug fix).\n\n3. Run, from the repo root, and report exact output:\n   - `node app/tools/validate-content.mjs`\n   - `node --test tools/audio-pipeline/qa-delivered-audio.test.mjs`\n   Both are read-only checks (verified: `qa-delivered-audio.test.mjs` only imports named functions from\n   `qa-delivered-audio.mjs`, whose file-writing `main()` is guarded behind an `import.meta.url` entrypoint\n   check and will not run on import). Confirm they pass, and note anything in their output the previous\n   author's report didn't mention.\n\n4. `git show a815245 --stat` and `git show a815245 -- app/app.js` to read the actual diff for the two\n   touched functions, rather than trusting the prose above — the prose is the previous author's own\n   description and could itself be wrong or incomplete.\n\n## Explicitly NOT in this slice\n\n- Do NOT edit any file. This is read-only review.\n- Do NOT run any `git` command that changes state (no commit, no checkout, no reset, no stash). `git show`\n  / `git log` / `git diff` (read-only forms) are fine.\n- Do NOT touch `app/content.json`, `app/images/**`, or anything under `tools/image-pipeline/`.\n- Do NOT attempt to start a dev server or open a browser — static/source review plus the two commands in\n  §3 only.\n\n## Report contents\n\n- A clear verdict: does the fix correctly close the gap described above, yes/no/partially.\n- Every discrepancy, edge case, mismatch, or missed call site you find — even minor ones — with exact\n  file:line references. If you find nothing wrong, say so explicitly and show the specific evidence that\n  ruled out each risk listed in §1, don't just assert confidence.\n- Full output of both commands from §3.\n- Confirmation of what you actually read/ran (don't summarize away — list file paths and line ranges).\n\n---\n\nIn scope:         Read-only review of app/app.js, app/content.json, tools/audio-pipeline/qa-delivered-audio.mjs,\n                  tools/audio-pipeline/qa-delivered-audio.test.mjs, app/tools/validate-content.mjs, and\n                  `git show a815245`. Running the two commands in §3. The report file.\n\nOut of scope:     Every other action. No edits anywhere. No git state changes.\n\nScope globs:\n- (none — this slice makes no file edits; the only expected output is the report file itself)\n\nKnown generated side effects: none expected (see the import.meta.url guard note in §3).\n\nAdd-dir required: none\n\nAcceptance gates: node app/tools/validate-content.mjs && node --test tools/audio-pipeline/qa-delivered-audio.test.mjs\n\nContext to read:  app/app.js (functions listed above), app/content.json (spot checks only),\n                  tools/audio-pipeline/qa-delivered-audio.mjs, tools/audio-pipeline/qa-delivered-audio.test.mjs,\n                  ai-system/projects/ajamix/CURRENT_STATE.md Part 30 (the author's own account of this fix,\n                  for comparison only — do not treat it as ground truth)\n\nReport to:        /Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-28-slice-29-report.md\n\nConstraints:      No new dependencies. No secrets. Stop and report rather than guess if something is\n                  genuinely ambiguous.\n\nRollback notes:   N/A — no edits made in this slice.\n\nHuman approval gates: This is a review-only slice with no changes to approve. If you find a real bug,\n                  report it in detail; do not attempt to fix it yourself.\n## Verdict: Partially\n\nThe core bug is fixed correctly for the current corpus: formal downloads and segmented playback now use the exact same three `audio/<moduleId>-01/-02/-03.mp3` strings.\n\nTwo cleanup limitations were missed:\n\n- Legacy `audio/<moduleId>.mp3` cache rows created by the buggy downloader are not migrated or removed. They can remain orphaned.\n- IndexedDB deletion failures are silently swallowed, while the returned count/bytes are calculated before deletion, so cleanup may claim a row was deleted when it remains ([app.js](/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/app/app.js:8399)).\n\nA schema edge case also remains: downloading accepts any non-empty `segments` array ([app.js](/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/app/app.js:6920)), whereas segmented playback requires exactly three ([app.js](/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/app/app.js:3856)). The validator prevents this in current content.\n\n### Evidence\n\n- All 359 formal modules have exactly three valid segment paths.\n- All paths exactly match `audio/<id>-01.mp3`, `-02.mp3`, `-03.mp3`.\n- All 359 retain unchanged legacy `audio/<id>.mp3` values compared with `a815245^`.\n- Playback passes the unmodified segment string from `getFormalSegmentAudioFile()` to the primary IndexedDB lookup ([app.js](/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/app/app.js:4021), [app.js](/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/app/app.js:6236)).\n- There are no case, slash, prefix, index-base, or zero-padding transformations in that path.\n- No generated download label collides with another module ID, activity ID, or generated label.\n- Vocational URL resolution remains `module.lessons[].audioFile`.\n- Current vocational labelling is unchanged because all 30 modules yield five URLs. Hypothetically, a one-URL vocational module would now receive a bare ID instead of `-01`.\n- Cleanup attempts all three segment URLs for a completed current formal module. It uses URL keys, so the metadata `moduleId` suffix is irrelevant.\n- No other active formal-segment call site reads legacy `module.audioFile`. Remaining direct reads belong to legacy fallback lessons, caregiver activities, or vocational lessons.\n\n### Acceptance-command output\n\n`node app/tools/validate-content.mjs` — exit 0:\n\n```text\nvalidate-content: OK — 389 module(s) pass.\n  track=vocational: 30\n  track=formal:     359\n  isChainLeaf:      362\n  chainNext set:    27\n```\n\n`node --test tools/audio-pipeline/qa-delivered-audio.test.mjs` — exit 0:\n\n```text\nPASS formal 149.9s fails\nPASS formal 150s passes\nPASS formal 330s passes\nPASS formal 331s fails\nPASS formal segment 2.9s fails\nPASS formal segment 3s passes\nPASS formal segment 90s passes\nPASS formal segment 90.1s fails\nPASS formal segment and legacy formal paths classify correctly\nPASS adult 2.9s fails\nPASS adult 3s passes\nPASS adult 40s passes\nPASS adult 40.1s fails\nPASS vocational valid path classifies and passes\nPASS falsafa valid path classifies and passes\nPASS criticalThinking valid path classifies and passes\nPASS unknown path fails classification\nPASS adult bitrate check still fails\nPASS adult mono check still fails\nPASS adult filename check still fails\nPASS worklist enumerates 1,077 formal segment targets and preserves 150 adult card targets\nAll deterministic delivered-audio QA tests passed.\n✔ tools/audio-pipeline/qa-delivered-audio.test.mjs (69.399167ms)\nℹ tests 1\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 1\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 76.963167\n```\n\nPart 30 described this as “20/20 pass,” but Node’s runner reports one test file/test; the named assertions printed by the file all passed.\n\n### Read/ran\n\n- [app.js](/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/app/app.js:3743): lines 3743–4085, 4200–4250, 4600–4640, 6180–6375, 6850–6960, 7140–7340, 7540–7595, 7970–8145, 8330–8465, 8940–9125, plus every `audioFile` occurrence.\n- [content.json](/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/app/content.json:85): lines 1–255, 4203–4250, 4376–4406, plus corpus-wide JSON audits.\n- [validate-content.mjs](/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/app/tools/validate-content.mjs:1): entire file, lines 1–281.\n- [qa-delivered-audio.mjs](/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/tools/audio-pipeline/qa-delivered-audio.mjs:1): entire file, lines 1–221. Its file-writing `main()` is correctly entrypoint-guarded.\n- [qa-delivered-audio.test.mjs](/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/tools/audio-pipeline/qa-delivered-audio.test.mjs:1): entire file, lines 1–79.\n- `CURRENT_STATE.md`: Part 30, lines 1642–1669.\n- `git show a815245 --stat`, `git show a815245 -- app/app.js`, parent function versions, and parent/current legacy-field comparison.\n\n`git show` returned the requested data but emitted sandbox warnings about being unable to create `/tmp/xcrun_db-*` cache files. The commit stat showed 50 files changed, 22,432 insertions, and 3,415 deletions.\n\n### Report-file blocker\n\nThe completed report could not be saved to:\n\n`/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-28-slice-29-report.md`\n\nThe write was rejected with:\n\n```text\nwriting is bl